  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NESA Center Combating Transnational Threats Senior Executive Seminar 02-23: &quot;Countering Narratives of Extremist Organizations: Managing Disinformation&quot;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CTSES 02-23 &quot;Countering Narratives of Extremist Organizations: Managing Disinformation&quot; The dangers posed by violent extremist organizations throughout the world remain potent and alarming. Many states in the NESA region have undertaken strong measures to degrade, isolate, and destroy these organizations but many of these still exist and some even are thriving. The violent extremist organizations have adapted and used technological advances, new media platforms, and new areas of operations to their advantage. Ineffective or insufficient legal and law enforcement measures at both domestic and international level further hamper countering extremism efforts. This seminar will analyze the scope and extent of the challenge posed by extremist narratives and facilitate conversations on lessons learnt from effective campaigns both in the hard and soft power domains especially in terms of countering extremist narratives. We will especially focus on how these extremist groups organize, recruit, utilize different means of communication, including disinformation campaigns, and build their nefarious narratives so as to think about strategies required to countering these efforts. This seminar seeks to build capacity and enhance regional partnerships in this arena. This seminar will explore both the nature of these challenges and think of creative solutions to build peace, resolve lingering conflicts, and enhance stability in the region.</narrative>
  </description>
